---
title: Getting started
description: Get an invitation, create an account, and open the dashboard.
---

# Getting started

The FIRST Global Simulator uses invitation-only accounts so administrators can gradually grow access and support participants.

## Request access

If you do not already have an invitation code, select **Request Invite** on the [home page](/). Share your name, team or organization, and email address so the Team Vietnam maintainers can follow up.

An administrator may also send a code directly. Invitation codes are one-time use, so keep yours private until you are ready to register.

## Create your account

Open [Sign in](/auth) and select **Register**. Enter your name, team, email, password, and invitation code.

After a successful registration, the simulator signs you in and sends you to the dashboard. If you tried to open a protected page first, you return to that page after sign-in.

> If a code is rejected, check its six characters carefully. A code may already have been redeemed, revoked, or expired. Ask the person who issued it for a replacement if needed.

## Open the dashboard

The [dashboard](/dashboard) is the starting point for the simulator experience. From there you can:

- create a FGC 2026 match lobby;
- open the offline sandbox;
- enter the [Robot Builder](/robot) to create a robot before future match play.

Use **Sign out** in the protected-page header when you finish on a shared device.
